# Lettre de motivation, ArenaNet, Contract UE5 Lighting Artist (7 October 2026)

Base : lettre adaptée avec mention des jeux de simulation (Santa Simulator, Bakery Coffee Simulator, Pet Grooming Simulator avec Meerkat Studio) et Noyes (jeu étudiant). (7 October 2026)

## English (7 October 2026)

To the recruitment team,

Hello ArenaNet,

I am writing about your opening for Contract UE5 Lighting Artist.

Lighting landscapes and crafting believable outdoor atmosphere in Unreal Engine 5 is at the heart of what I do. Taking an environment through a full dynamic day/night cycle, balancing exposure, volumetric fog and sky art while preserving visual clarity for gameplay is a challenge I genuinely enjoy.

My name is Matthieu Huguet, I am 25 and I work as a freelance Technical Artist and 3D Artist, based in Aix-en-Provence, France.

I studied a Game Design Bachelor at LISAA Paris, a Master's at ARTFX Montpellier, then technical art courses at Gnomon and through Harvard CS50, before going freelance in early 2025.

In production, I worked as a freelance Technical Artist with Meerkat Studio on three simulation titles: Santa Simulator (shipped on Steam), Bakery Coffee Simulator (shipped on Steam), and Pet Grooming Simulator (paid contract). Earlier in my studies, I co-developed Noyes (student game). I also completed an archviz lighting project for a private client in Aix-en-Provence. All my work can be seen at matthieuhuguet.com.

My workflow connects Houdini and Unreal Engine 5: building procedural assets and sky elements (such as clouds, celestial bodies and height maps) in Houdini, then integrating them directly into Unreal Engine with Lumen, custom materials and light functions. My latest published work includes Ceramic Tiles (crafted with Houdini Copernicus and Unreal Lumen), Fleur de Lys, Procedural Lily, and HDA Stairs Component.

Your opening for UE5 Lighting Artist lines up directly with my day-to-day focus: real-time PBR lighting, atmospheric scattering, custom shaders and performance optimization.

What I am looking for today is a contract with a team committed to an ambitious world like Guild Wars. I need to work with experienced professionals and be part of a collective dynamic, something that working solo, however formative, cannot provide.

I am available for contract work immediately on a remote basis, invoicing as an independent contractor from France.

I would be happy to talk with you by phone or video call, whenever suits you.

Matthieu Huguet
